SUMMARY:One Last Backcountry Weekend in Frontenac
DESCRIPTION:Wilderness Union Toronto - Outdoor Adventure and Hiking Club\n
 **Please note the only way to register for this adventure is on [our websi
 te.](https://www.wildernessunion.com/adventures/weekend-in-frontenac)**\n\
 n**Fall (aka shoulder season) camping brings the serene beauty of the back
 country\, without the crowds and bugs.**\n\nAt this time of year\, Fronten
 ac will be less busy and the trail into Big Clear Lake belongs mostly to u
 s. It's a 9km hike to reach the site\, working through root tangled trails
  and stretches of open granite typical of this stretch of the Canadian Shi
 eld. Only the most stubborn leaves will remain on the trees and you’ll e
 njoy long sightlines through bare branches where the canopy used to be. Th
 e pace is steady and moderate the whole way in\, never technical but never
  quite letting up either.\n\nWe set up camp on the shore of Big Clear Lake
  as the light starts to drop\, we get a fire going\, and cook dinner toget
 her. Late October nights out here are serene\, with a sky full of stars ov
 er the lake.\n\nIn the morning\, we’ll take our time over breakfast befo
 re packing up and heading out along the other side of Big Salmon Lake: a d
 ifferent stretch of trail from the one we hiked in on\, with its own look 
 at the park before we're back where we started.\n\nBy the time we're back 
 at the cars\, you'll have had that sweet final night of the year in the ba
 ckcountry.\n\nWhat's included\n\n* Professional & certified guides\n* ‍A
 ll camp meals\, cooking equipment and mess kits\n* ‍Tents\n\nSleeping ba
 gs and sleep pads can be rented from WU for a small fee.\n\n**Accessibilit
 y**\nWilderness Union is committed to making our adventures as accessible 
 as possible. If you wish to make an accommodation request relating to a di
 sability or provide feedback\, please do so by sending an email to info@wi
 ldernessunion.com\n\n**Highlights**\n**Last Trip of the Season:** The fina
 l overnight on the calendar before WU's backcountry program pauses for win
 ter\n**Shoulder Season Solitude**: Long\, quiet stretches of trail\, with 
 the lake mostly to yourselves.\n**A Clear Night Sky:** Bare branches and d
 ry autumn air make for some of the best stargazing conditions of the year 
 at the campsite.\n\n**Event cost: $265+HST. $70 optional transport also av
 ailable. Please register [here.](https://www.wildernessunion.com/adventure
 s/weekend-in-frontenac)**\n\n**About Wilderness Union**\nWilderness Union 
 is deliberate about building an outdoors community that connects you to th
 e life-changing magic of the outdoors and helps you find your people.\n\nM
 embers range from 20-40 years old. The group is a mix of GTA locals and ne
 wcomers to Toronto from within Canada and abroad.\n\nAttendance numbers on
  Meetup don't reflect our actual event attendance - we typically have 15-2
 0 community members at each event. Large enough that there's someone new t
 o meet but small enough that it's not overwhelming!\n\n***Learn more at ou
 r website [www.wildernessunion.com](https://www.wildernessunion.com/)***
